# Air wing and airbase selection, reworked for 2560x1440 (A1, redesigned 2026-10-16).
# Overrides eight top-level windows of vanilla interface/airselectionview.gui; the vanilla file stays in place
# and supplies every other window. The untouched vanilla text of each window is in baseline/airselectionview/.
#
# Compared with vanilla:
#   - the panel is an 820 px stack of cards: a header plate (818x108) with a Missions card and five toolbar
#     plates, then the list frame unassigned_airwings_view (818 wide, 19 rows of 48 before it scrolls instead
#     of 9). The plates are icons drawn behind widgets that stay direct children of their vanilla windows.
#   - the mission bar keeps its code-set width (slots x slotsize.width + 2 x position.x) on a transparent
#     background; the Missions card under it has a fixed 806 px, so the panel width no longer follows the DLC.
#     Slots are 52 instead of 45, so 15 missions fill the card.
#   - airbase, wing, gun emplacement and rocket rows are 784 wide instead of 548, in fixed columns: aircraft
#     0-207, mission efficiency 210, name (hoi_20b) and status (hoi_18mbs) at 240 with 282 px each, mission
#     icons at 530, orders 640-747. The close buttons of the toolbar and of every row share one column.
#   - the airbase row has a "Capacity" caption (vanilla key UNIT_LEADER_CAPACITY_SORT) and 220 px for the name
#   - hotkeys shift+n on create air group and shift+u on unassign
#   - the quick deploy popup is 900 high instead of 515, with a one size larger font
guiTypes = {
	containerWindowType = {
		name = "air_selection_view"
		position = {x=0 y=77}
		size = { width=820 height=1056 } # height set in code, but initial value here is used for max allowed height
